From 5e3fd22ed6449d52fa2c48a204c5a70ac74c9046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:29:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0256 -- OPL window pacing is off by default, a
 detected PicoGUS included

WHY: the confirmation cell for patch 0255 on the landed build (dosags
LAB-JOURNEYS 8.49, PACEL, round P) failed a HEALTH row: 4 silent SB IRQs
against a limit of 3. Every other row passed: TIMER, engagement, peak bound,
late 0, cap 0, underruns 0, overwrites 0, SB alive, isr_max 7.8 ms. The
pre-registered consequence (8.43 amendment 1) is that a health-row failure
turns the PicoGUS pacing default OFF pending investigation, because the
default reaches every PicoGUS player. Off is the conservative direction: it
restores the pre-0255 player behaviour. Whether pacing causes the extra
silent IRQ is not established. It sat at the intro's first play of a sound,
and silent counts there vary by more than 1 run to run. A same-binary on/off
ABBA settles it (LAB-JOURNEYS 8.50).

WHAT: SDL_DOSMidiDeferEnable's default K is 0 on every card, where it was
128 for a detected PicoGUS. SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_K=N (16..1024) still turns
pacing on at K=N, and SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_WINDOW_US still sets the window.
The peak-arrival witness and everything else in 0255 is unchanged. It is a
default flip, not a re-tune. A restore-default patch comes back only with the
ABBA's evidence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h | 2 +-
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h
index 3593ab909..e61d97930 100644
--- a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h
@@ -296,7 +296,7 @@ extern SDL_DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL_DOSMidiDeferStats4(Uint32 *dedupe_on, Uint3
    reads = dummy status reads after each address and data write. */
 extern SDL_DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL_DOSOplPacing(Uint32 *pgdetect, Uint32 *reads);
 /* DOS-PORT patch 0255: OPL arrival pacing and its witness. k = writes allowed per
-   window (0 = off; 128 by default on a detected PicoGUS, else 0;
+   window (0 = off; 0 by default on every card since patch 0256, a detected PicoGUS included;
    SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_K), win_us = the window (default 2570, one PicoGUS
    drain period; SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_WINDOW_US), waits and wait_us / wait_max_us
    = the pacing waits taken and their time (included in 0250's isr_sum),
diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 69bbb753f..7899b00ab 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -2249,12 +2249,14 @@ bool SDL_DOSMidiDeferEnable(int kind)
         const char *e = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOS_MIDI_DEFER_DRAIN_STI");
         g_mdq_drain_sti = (e && e[0] == '0' && e[1] == 0) ? 0 : 1;
     }
-    { /* DOS-PORT patch 0255: window pacing -- on for a detected PicoGUS, off elsewhere.
+    { /* DOS-PORT patch 0255: window pacing -- off by default (0256; was on for a detected PicoGUS).
          SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_K=0 turns it off, N (16..1024) sets K on any OPL;
          SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_WINDOW_US (500..20000) sets the window. */
         const char *e = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_K");
         const char *w = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_WINDOW_US");
-        Uint32 k = (kind == 1 && g_dos_opl_pgdetect == 1) ? 128u : 0u;
+        /* DOS-PORT patch 0256: off by default everywhere, a detected PicoGUS included, pending the
+           investigation of dosags LAB-JOURNEYS 8.49 (the hint still turns it on). */
+        Uint32 k = 0u;
         Uint32 win = 2570u;
         if (e && *e) {
             const long v = SDL_strtol(e, NULL, 10);
-- 
